deabad35 (1584 1793457988014 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f344") (src . "test: fixture helpers judge an insert answer's head before reading it\n\nTwo fixtures read the cdr of a write's answer as an alist without first\nlooking at its head. A refused write answers (error unknown\n(commit-barrier-failed) ...), which is what a store answers when the fsync\nbarrier of a commit fails, and the assq on that list raised \"improperly\nformed alist\". In test/daemon-namespace.sc the raise ended the run at W5p\nwith the rows after it never reached; in test/change-stream.sc it reached\nthe scheduler, which ends the process at once with exit 70 and the row's\ndaemon still running, so the fixture's teardown was skipped and a daemon\nsurvived in its namespace under the scratch root.\n\ntest/daemon-namespace.sc: hold-a-write! judges the head of the insert's\nfirst datum. On a non-ok answer it starts no write and returns\n(refused <answer>); W5p binds that value and compares it with #t, as W5l6\nalready did, so a refused insert reads as one red row with the answer in\nits FAIL line and the run goes on to its teardown.\n\ntest/change-stream.sc: new-id and mark-of judge the head and, on a non-ok\nanswer, keep it in a run-level refusals list (refused!, once however many\nhelpers read the same answer) and return #f. want-1 fails the next check\nwhenever that list is non-empty and prints the kept answers, so a row whose\nown comparison comes out right on a store that refused its write still\nreads red. frame-settled answers (no-mark) at once when it is given no\nmark, before reading any frame. The rows run under a guard\n(start-scheduler-with-teardown): a raise outside a check prints one FAIL\nline and any kept refusals, sends TERM and, a second later, KILL to every\nprocess whose command line names one of this run's daemon runner scripts,\nprints the rows and failures lines and exits 1 instead of leaving the process to the scheduler's exit 70.\n\nEvidence, from the fixtures run alone with the fault\nfsync-fail@commit:file=000001.sexp on one daemon (each probe is a copy of\nthe fixture with the fault added to one daemon's start line; the probes\nare archived, not rows): on the old tree\ndaemon-namespace stopped at W5p with 20 rows and no completion line, and\nchange-stream ended at PROBE-07 with exit 70 and two processes left; on\nthe new tree W5p and PROBE-07 read red with the refusal printed, both\nfixtures print their completion line (118 and 131 rows) and no process is\nleft. A variant of want-1 that ignores the refusals list reads ACCEPT-4\ngreen under the same fault, so the list alone is what reds a row that\nsurvives a refusal. A probe with the FRAME block's daemon faulted ended\nthe run at FRAME-01 before mark-of was guarded and reds FRAME-01..08 with\nthe run completing after it.\n\ntest/rows-baseline.txt: the two fixtures' hashes; row and line counts\nunchanged (change-stream 131/164, daemon-namespace 118/122).\n\nStage on an isolated copy of the tree (238 fixtures): only the known pair\nred (f0-ondemand COST-1 over its budget, startup-ratio C1/C3); change-stream\n131/0, daemon-namespace 118/0; row baseline hashes all the described\nversions; no process of the run left; alternation of the compiled product\nagainst the base median 1.0017 (p10 ratios 1.0017, 1.0042, 0.9958), within\n1%. Reviewed in two rounds; the second round added the head check in\nmark-of, the no-mark answer of frame-settled, refused! keeping an answer\nonce, and the guard's refused line.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 568))))
